functional Interface what is this  -> A functional interface in Java is an interface that has only one abstract method,
becose it has just one method so that it will be implimented using the lamda expression 


Predicate ->Functional Interface: The Predicate<T> interface has a single abstract method, boolean 
test(T t), which evaluates a condition on the given argument and returns true or false

Predicate<Integer> isGreaterThanFive = number -> number > 5;
System.out.println(isGreaterThanFive.test(10));

Function (functional interface ) -> The Function functional interface is a specific built-in type defined in the java.util.function package that represents a function which accepts one argument and produces a result

// Function that takes an Integer and returns its square (as an Integer)
Function<Integer, Integer> square = x -> x * x;
System.out.println(square.apply(5));

